for shows as dark and suspenseful as  ncis it's hard to imagine one scene's  subject matter seeming harder to watch  than the rest so what event could be so  heart-wrenching that it outshines an  entire season keep watching to discover  the one scene ncis season 9 took too far  as sad as it is to see familiar faces  leave one universal truth has emerged  ncis likes to craft dramatic exits for  its characters as time has gone on  audiences have gotten used to living  with the worry that something terrible  could happen to their favorite  investigator at any moment packed with  ups downs major plot twists and plenty  of ncis classic brand of drama season 9  is no exception to this gruesome  storytelling style in it we see  everything from tony denozzo played by  michael weatherly getting shot to cody  de pablo's character is eva david  receiving a marriage proposal in crime  dramas like ncis there are plenty of  scenes that may be difficult for some  audiences to watch especially while  experiencing the rest of the emotional  turmoil included in season 9. however  there is one particular scene involving  a major character that is almost too  shocking to talk about in ncis season 9  episode 24 tell death do us part it's  not a grisly crime scene or awkward  moment that leaves viewers reeling  instead audiences get a taste of this  show's trademark heartbreak when at the  end of this action-packed season finale  fan-favorite medical examiner donald  ducky mallard played by david mcgallum  has a heart attack the shocking event is  one of many packed into the hour-long  season finale and its placement in the  latter half of the episode only adds to  the tension till death do us part sees  gibbs and his team pull out all the  stops as they continue to investigate a  series of deadly explosions gibbs  recruits dr samantha ryan portrayed by  guest star jaime lee curtis to help  identify the cause soon a man named  harper dearing played by richard schiff  becomes the focus of the ncis team's  investigation in the final act deering's  last bomb goes off right outside ncis  headquarters the scene would be dramatic  enough by itself but it's only made  worse by the fact that gibbs mcgee ziva  dinozzo and abby are all trapped inside  by the damage in the episode's final  scene ducky is seen walking along the  beach as he takes in the view he  receives a call presumably about the  fatal bombing ducky demands that nobody  touches the bodies of the deceased then  pauses as a heart attack strikes  it's imperative that no one touch any of  the deceased until i  until i re  the last image of the season 9 finale  shows ducky collapsed on the beach as  the tide rolls in the heart attack seems  to be the result of overwhelming stress  from the shocking phone call and  audiences are left to wonder about  ducky's fate and the fate of all his  trapped team members the ncis season 9  finale ends so dramatically the fact  that it is stuck in the minds of fans  almost a decade after it aired should  come as no great surprise in june 2021  when a reddit user posed the question  any episodes of ncis that made you cry  fans had no trouble coming up with  plenty of iconic moments that hit a  little too close to home even still  ducky's heart attack made many viewers  list despite the 18 seasons of drama  they had to pick from when the thread  was posted a redditor included the scene  in their top three along with the deaths  of gibb's father and palmer's wife the  commenter went out to clarify there are  more that hug at the heart but these  three made me cry ducky is a vital  character in the series whose charm and  random educational banter has fans fully  invested in his well-being so watching  him have a heart attack in the ninth  season finale of ncis was a scene that  was a bit too much for some audience  members to handle  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe t